      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not put butter or lotion on a burn, as this can trap heat and make the injury worse. You need to cool the burn immediately by running cool (not ice-cold) water over the affected area for at least ten minutes. After cooling, cover the burn loosely with a sterile, non-stick bandage. If the pain is severe, a large, blistering burn, or if you are concerned, seek medical attention right away.",
